{
  "$comment": "The shared rule set: rules every linter family implements, under each family's own name. Sources: ESLint core rules (eslint/use-at-your-own-risk builtinRules), oxlint --rules (eslint scope, not type aware), deno lint --rules, and Biome's own mapping from `biome migrate eslint`, asked one rule at a time. eslint names the typescript-eslint extension where one exists, as a TypeScript project would. biomeOptions are the options `biome migrate eslint` writes for ESLint's defaults. Left out: no-cond-assign, no-throw-literal and no-invalid-regexp (no Biome rule), no-undef (each linter has its own globals), no-with and no-delete-var (sloppy mode only; Biome maps no-delete-var to noDelete, which forbids every delete). Also left out, because `rules verify` showed they mean different things: no-inner-declarations (ESLint 9 and oxlint report nothing in ES modules by default, Deno and Biome report function declarations in blocks) and constructor-super (Biome checks invalid super() calls, not a missing one). Every rule has a fixture in fixtures/rules/<id>.* that `pnpm arena rules verify` lints with every family.",
